1
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,770
弗里曼：50年前，在苏格兰
(Freeman) 50 years ago in Scotland,

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:05,880
有个人脑袋里冒出了个妙主意
one man had a brilliant idea --

3
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:10,580
从这个主意开始 欧美的众多科学家们
an idea that today pits science detectives in Europe and America

4
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:11,950
彼此竞争
against each other

5
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:14,820
涉及百亿美元的金钱 为了解开一个谜团
in a $10 billion race to solve the riddle

6
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:18,330
那就是，你，我以及周遭万物
of what you,me,and everything around us

7
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:20,090
究竟由何组成
is really made of.

8
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:24,000
这是深入物质核心之旅
It's a journey into the heart of matter,

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,030
俯冲进入我们的物理存在
plunging into the core of our physical being

10
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:30,300
以及物理世界本身的核心
and of the physical world itself.

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,110
进入亚原子宇宙的旅程
But will this journey into the subatomic Universe

12
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:36,840
会给我们对自然界的认识 带来革命性的变化吗？
revolutionize our understanding of nature,

13
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:39,910
或者，只是向我们揭示
or will it reveal just how little we really know

14
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:43,180
我们对自身是什么 由何组成这一问题的无知
about who we are and what we're made of?

15
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:52,030
空间，时间，生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

16
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:58,330
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

17
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:01,330
♪穿越虫洞 第1x07集♪
♪Through the Wormhole 1x07♪

18
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:05,740
我们究竟由何组成？
What Are We Really Made Of?

19
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:09,510
我们究竟由何组成-
What are we really made of --

20
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:13,780
你，我，还有身边万物？
you,me,everything around us?

21
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:16,650
这个简单的问题
That simple question has kept people guessing

22
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:18,920
困扰了人类几千年
for thousands of years.

23
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,990
在古代 答案很简单
In ancient times,the answer was easy --

24
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:23,760
万事万物都由4种基本元素中的
everything in creation was made

25
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:27,330
1种或几种组成
from one or more of the four elements --

26
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:28,830
土...
Earth...

27
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:30,900
气...
Air...

28
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:32,500
火...
Fire...

29
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,970
水
and Water.

30
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:39,310
当我小时候 当然，还不是那么古老的年代
When I was a kid,in not quite so ancient times,

31
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:42,880
我们被教育说 万物都是由原子构成的
we were told that everything is made out of atoms.

32
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,880
但在最近的几十年里
But in the last few decades,

33
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,750
科学家们研究原子内部
scientists have looked inside the atom

34
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:51,250
发现事情真相复杂的多
and found that things are a lot more complicated.

35
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:53,320
先把我们的知识放一边
Despite all of our knowledge,

36
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:57,020
我们仍然并不完全了解 物质自然的真相
we still don't understand the true nature of matter.

37
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,290
但是现在
But right now,

38
00:01:58,290 --> 00:02:01,230
数千个调查员追踪着线索
thousands of investigators are following hunches,

39
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:03,000
跟踪嫌疑人
tracking down suspects,

40
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,760
已经前所未有的接近目标
and getting closer than ever

41
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:07,800
搞清楚我们和 身边的东东西西
to learning how we and everything around us

42
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,500
如何组成
fits together.

43
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,740
他们的研究方法是 打碎它（很黄很暴力）
And they're doing it by breaking things apart.

44
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:17,080
当我6岁时
When I was 6 years old,

45
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:20,550
我老爹把他的旧怀表给了我
my father gave me his old pocket watch --

46
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:22,120
一个计时器
a time keeper.

47
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:25,590
"这玩艺是咋么工作滴?" 我很好奇
"How does this work?" I wondered.

48
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:28,460
我决心找出真相
I decided to find out.

49
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:34,430
把它拆开很容易 困难的是怎么再次组合起来
Taking it apart was a lot easier than putting it back together,

50
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:38,700
但是我学到了一点东西 关于滴答计时的奥秘
but I learned a little about what makes things tick.

51
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:42,870
现代的粒子物理学家 搞得也是这一套
And that's pretty much what particle physicists do today.

52
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:46,210
他们把东西撞碎
They smash things up and look at the debris

53
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:49,310
然后通过超强的显微镜 检查残骸
through extremely powerful microscopes.

54
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:50,610
我们像小孩子一样
We do what kids do.

55
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:53,210
我们把东西撞碎 然后看看会搞出什么东西
We smash things,and we look to see what comes out.

56
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:54,550
为了达到这个目的
And so,to do that,

57
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:57,180
我们需要更强、更强、更强的撞击
we need to smash things harder and harder and harder

58
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,750
来观察更小、更小、更小的物体
to see what's smaller and smaller and smaller.

59
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:03,560
弗里曼：位于芝加哥的Argon国家实验室
(Freeman) At Chicago's Argon National Laboratory,

60
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:08,260
Bob Stanek建造了通向 亚原子世界的机器
Bob Stanek builds machines that peer into the subatomic world.

61
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:11,630
呃，这是我们的先进光子源-
So,this is our advanced photon source --

62
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:15,400
一个周长大概半英里的显微镜
a microscope that's about a half a mile around,

63
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:20,210
包括33个站点
and it contains 33 stations

64
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:23,610
意味着可以开展33项独立试验
where 33 individual experiments can go on

65
00:03:23,610 --> 00:03:25,710
测量微小的结构
measuring tiny structures

66
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:29,380
或者测量这些家伙感兴趣的东西
of whatever these guys feel happy measuring.

67
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,920
如果你还记得高中时代
If you remember way back in High School,

68
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,660
通过显微镜观察微小物体
when you looked through the microscope

69
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:38,930
你说"哇，看看这些东东 多么滴小巧啊"
and you said,"wow,look at all that stuff -- how neat it is,"

70
00:03:38,930 --> 00:03:43,860
普通的光线和透镜能给你 展现如此的细节
it's amazing that ordinary light and optics

71
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:46,700
这真是一个奇迹
can bring you to such a detailed level.

72
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:50,270
然而，对如今的许多事物
However,for a lot of things nowadays,

73
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:52,840
你需要比普通光线 更多的条件
you need more than just that ordinary light.

74
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:55,580
你需要观察 更小、更小、更小的世界
You need to get smaller and smaller and smaller.

75
00:03:58,210 --> 00:04:01,310
利用A.P.S 我们可以看到
With the A.P.S.,we can see things much smaller

76
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:04,420
以往通过普通显微镜 看不到的东西
than we could see with our standard microscope.

77
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:07,220
我们可以把物体放大10倍
We could see things a factor of 10 smaller,

78
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:10,660
一千倍 一万倍
a factor of 1,000 smaller,a factor of 10,000 smaller.

79
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:14,290
实际上 与普通的光学显微镜相比
In fact,we can see things that are 10 to the 10th smaller

80
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:17,100
我们能看到 放大百亿倍的物体
than what we could see with ordinary light.

81
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,600
我们可以看到分子
We can see molecules.

82
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,930
看到病毒
We can see viruses.

83
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:22,970
我们几乎可以看到生命的结构
We can almost see the structur of life.

84
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:28,540
弗里曼： 能够给分子和原子照相 这真是不得了的能力
(Freeman) The ability to take pictures of molecules and atoms

85
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:32,580
因为仅在100年前
is an incredible thing,because only 100 years ago,

86
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,550
原子还只是一种理论
the atom was just a theory.

87
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:39,120
在20世纪初叶
At the dawn of the 20th century,

88
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:42,860
关于原子的说法是 如果真的存在原子
it was believed that if atoms existed at all,

89
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:47,090
它们要么是空壳 要么是实心小球
they were either empty shells or solid little balls.

90
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:52,030
一项研究改变了一切
Then one investigation changed everything.

91
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:55,600
卢瑟福的原子理论
It was the brainchild of Ernest Rutherford,

92
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:58,940
他是粒子物理学界的 夏洛克 福尔摩斯
the Sherlock Holmes of particle physics.

93
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:01,940
Steve Nahn是麻省理工教授
Steve Nahn is a Professor at M.I.T.

94
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:06,280
也是世界上最大粒子加速器 一个研究小组的头目
and a team leader on the world's biggest Particle Accelerator,

95
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:09,850
欧洲巨强子对撞机
the Large Hadron Collider in Europe.

96
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:11,520
Steve将会重现
Steve is going to reproduce

97
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,890
科学史上
one of the most important experiments

98
00:05:13,890 --> 00:05:15,590
最重要的试验之一
in the history of science --

99
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:20,660
卢瑟福对原子结构的探索
Rutherford's probe into the structure of the atom.

100
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,500
(Nahn) 这个实验 和卢瑟福做过的一样
(Nahn) This experiment is the same as Rutherford's experiment.

101
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:27,570
我们用同一种金箔
We use the same kind of gold foils

102
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:30,670
用上百万个粒子 打穿这些金箔
and send millions of particles through these gold foils.

103
00:05:30,670 --> 00:05:33,640
卢瑟福认为 这些粒子
Rutherford thought that all the particles

104
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,810
会直线穿过 基本上不产生偏斜
would essentially go straight through and not deflect at all,

105
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:39,810
但事实不是这样
but that's not what happened.

106
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:41,810
弗里曼：卢瑟福实验
(Freeman) The Rutherford experiment

107
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,350
就像冲着干草堆发射 带火的子弹
is like firing bullets at a haystack.

108
00:05:44,350 --> 00:05:46,750
粒子就像子弹
The particle are like bullets,

109
00:05:46,750 --> 00:05:50,420
而金箔中的原子就像干草堆
and the atoms in the gold foil are like haystacks.

110
00:05:51,730 --> 00:05:55,730
如果干草堆是空的 子弹当然直传而过
If the haystack is empty,the bullets go straight through.

111
00:05:56,800 --> 00:06:00,330
如果干草堆里包着加农炮弹
If the haystack is packed with cannonballs,

112
00:06:00,330 --> 00:06:02,540
子弹就会被反弹回来
all the bullets bounce back.

113
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:06,940
如果在中心存在 一些加农炮弹
If there are a few cannonballs in the center,

114
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:09,640
一部分子弹会反弹
some of the bullets will bounce back.

115
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:13,380
这就是实验中发生的情况
And that's what happened.

116
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:16,050
当卢瑟福发射他的粒子
When Rutherford fired his particles,

117
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:17,580
大部分直飞而过
most went straight through,

118
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:21,520
但是，某些粒子被从目标 中心强烈的反弹出来
but some sharply bounced back from the center of the target,

119
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:25,020
完全出乎当时的预料
upending the conceived wisdom of the time.

120
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:30,300
在那里，有某种又小又硬的东西
Something small and hard was down in there,

121
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:33,430
就在原子深处
deep inside the Shell of the atom.

122
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:38,640
这是证据，证明了 在原子的中心
This is the evidence for a very heavy,very small object

123
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,510
有一个非常重、非常小的物体
at the core of the atom --

124
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,280
高密度的原子核周围
the high-density nucleus

125
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:45,240
是巨大的空间
surrounded by a vastness of empty space.

126
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:46,810
弗里曼：实际上
(Freeman) In fact,

127
00:06:46,810 --> 00:06:50,750
原子核的直径只有 原子直径的
the nucleus of an atom is 100,000 times smaller

128
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,250
十万分之一
than its radius.

129
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:55,420
就像是在足球场中央
It's equivalent to the head of a pin

130
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:58,590
放了一个大头针的头儿
in the middle of a football stadium.

131
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:04,760
卢瑟福之后，物理学家们 继续向原子内部进军
After Rutherford,physicists probed further into the atom.

132
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:07,600
他们发现，原子包括3部分
They found that it is built out of three parts --

133
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:10,940
质子和中子组成了原子核
the protons and neutrons that form the nucleus

134
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:15,040
电子环绕着原子核
and the electrons that form the Shell around it.

135
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:18,810
在它们之间，构成了原子
Between them,they make up atoms.

136
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:23,220
原子组成分子
Atoms stick together and form molecules.

137
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:25,150
众多的分子
Out of the molecules,

138
00:07:25,150 --> 00:07:29,620
组成了复杂的结构 比如DNA...
we get more complex shapes,from a strand of DNA...

139
00:07:31,730 --> 00:07:35,330
...人体最多可包含
...Up to the 7,000 trillion,trillion atoms

140
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:37,400
七千万亿万亿个原子
that form a human body.

141
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:41,370
一段时期内，原子理论
For a time,the atomic theory of the Universe

142
00:07:41,370 --> 00:07:44,540
似乎解决了一切问题
seemed to explain most everything,

143
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:48,810
但是，科学家们开始 打破原子
but then physicists started breaking atoms apart,

144
00:07:48,810 --> 00:07:53,450
他们发现了大量神秘的新粒子
and they discovered a slew of mysterious new particles

145
00:07:53,450 --> 00:07:56,980
把原有的理论搅了个 天翻地覆
that turned their theories upside down.

146
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:01,350
最吓人的被称为反物质
The most frightening was called antimatter --

147
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:04,090
物质的邪恶孪生兄弟
matter's evil twin.

148
00:08:04,090 --> 00:08:08,690
如果这么多的反物质 接触到普通物质
If just this much touches ordinary matter,

149
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:10,530
能量足以夷平一座城市
it will level a city.

150
00:08:10,530 --> 00:08:14,600
为什么科学家们如此 致力于制造反物质?
So,why are scientists trying so hard to make it?

151
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:19,310
人们发现，它可能蕴含 物质之谜的秘密
Turns out it may hold the secret to the mystery of matter.

152
00:08:24,190 --> 00:08:27,060
当科学家第一次打碎原子
When scientists first smashed atoms apart,

153
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:30,300
他们发现了构成原子的材料-
they uncovered their essential building blocks --

154
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:34,240
质子，中子，电子
protons,neutrons,and electrons.

155
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,240
然后，他们建造了
Next,they built machines

156
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:39,980
能够将这些小粒子碰撞
that let them smash these tiny pieces together,

157
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:42,980
从而创造出奇怪的 新粒子的机器
and out came strange,new particles.

158
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:47,920
最奇怪的东西 恐怕要数我们称之为反物质的了
Perhaps the strangest is the stuff we call antimatter --

159
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,790
极性相反的物质
matter's polar opposite.

160
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:54,760
宇宙中最具爆炸性的东西
It's the most explosive substance in the Universe.

161
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:57,590
当物质与反物质相遇
When matter and antimatter touch,

162
00:08:57,590 --> 00:09:00,700
它们极其剧烈的互相消灭
they violently cancel each other out.

163
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:04,130
物理学家称之为"湮灭"
Physicists say,they annihilate each other.

164
00:09:04,130 --> 00:09:07,740
伴随着极其巨大的爆炸
It triggers an enormous explosion.

165
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:10,070
爆炸有多厉害？
How big of an explosion?

166
00:09:10,070 --> 00:09:14,040
不到半克的反物质
Less than half a gram of antimatter rice

167
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:17,050
可以产生13万吨当量的爆炸
would produce a 13-kiloton blast

168
00:09:17,050 --> 00:09:19,920
相当于广岛原子弹的威力
as big as the Hiroshima bomb.

169
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:29,360
Frank Close教授 理论物理学家
Professor Frank Close is a theoretical physicist

170
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,530
供职于牛津大学
at Oxford University.

171
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:35,530
[英国口音] 反物质正好是 物质的相对面
[ British accent ] Antimatter is a perfect opposite to matter.

172
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:38,870
如果我是反物质做成的
If I was made of antimatter,

173
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:42,800
我的行为和今天没啥两样
I would look exactly the same as I do today.

174
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,670
如果你仔细看看 组成我的那些原子
If you looked at the atoms that I'm made of,

175
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:50,580
它们看上去 和正常的原子也没什么不同
they would look exactly the same if I was made of antiatoms.

176
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:54,080
只有当你进入原子内部
It's only when you get inside the atoms

177
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,520
才能看出蹊跷
that you see the difference.

178
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:57,390
普通的原子中
That's the atoms that we're made of

179
00:09:57,390 --> 00:10:00,190
带负电荷的电子
have little negatively charged electrons

180
00:10:00,190 --> 00:10:03,930
围绕着带正电 体积、质量巨大的原子核运转
whirling around a big,bulky,positive nucleus.

181
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:11,100
(弗里曼)反物质呢？
(Freeman) And the antiatoms?

182
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,570
问这个男人
Ask this man --

183
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:14,430
Joel Fajans
Joel Fajans,

184
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,140
一位反物质研究者
an antimatter investigator

185
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:19,010
供职加州大学巴克利分校
at the University of California,Berkeley.

186
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:21,470
宇宙中，反物质到处都是
Antimatter is everywhere in the Universe.

187
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:24,680
举个例子，这个香蕉中 存在钾40
For instance,this banana contains potassium 40,

188
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:28,620
钾的一种同位素 能够放射出正电子
an isotope of potassium which emits positrons.

189
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:31,220
正电子和其它粒子 构成了反物质
Positrons and other forms of antimatter

190
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:34,490
困难的研究对象 但正是我的工作
are difficult to study,however,and that's my job.

191
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:38,090
这就是我所做的 研究反物质
That's what I do,is to study antimatter.

192
00:10:38,090 --> 00:10:40,230
那边的那个试验
I was partially inspired to do this

193
00:10:40,230 --> 00:10:42,000
给予了我极大的鼓励—
by this experiment over here --

194
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,400
质子加速器
the Bevatron Accelerator

195
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:46,030
位于劳伦斯 巴克利 国家实验室
at the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory.

196
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:50,770
质子加速器是第一个 巨粒子加速器
The Bevatron was the first giant Particle Accelerator.

197
00:10:50,770 --> 00:10:54,440
现在已经很破旧了 但是在上世纪50年代
It's being torn apart now,but back in the '50s,

198
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:57,710
它可是世界物理研究的中心
it was the center of the world for physics research.

199
00:10:57,710 --> 00:11:00,710
质子加速器所采用的
The same techniques that were used in the Bevatron

200
00:11:00,710 --> 00:11:02,120
加速粒子的方法
to accelerate particles

201
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:05,220
现在被用于遍布全世界的
are now used in the enormous Particle Accelerators

202
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,050
各种巨粒子加速器
that are throughout the world.

203
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:13,660
弗里曼：粒子加速器 有点像巨大的显微镜
(Freeman) Particle Accelerators are like giant microscopes

204
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:16,800
是我们能够观察亚原子世界
that let us peer into the subatomic world.

205
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:21,430
它们将物质打碎为 最小的部件
They break matter down into its smallest components.

206
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:25,070
要想探测到反物质
Drilling down far enough to detect antimatter

207
00:11:25,070 --> 00:11:28,140
需要从原子核中取出质子
requires taking protons from an atom's nucleus,

208
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,380
将它们束缚在真空中
trapping them in a vacuum,

209
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:35,180
然后将它们射入 一个有巨大电磁场的环中
then shooting them into a ring of giant electromagnets.

210
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:37,150
一个粒子加速器是以
So,a Particle Accelerator works

211
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:41,950
在环中做圆周运动的质子开始的
by starting protons going around in a circle in a ring.

212
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:43,890
质子每转一圈
And every time they go around,

213
00:11:43,890 --> 00:11:46,490
你利用电场给它们增加点动力
you give them a little kick with an electric field

214
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:49,600
于是它们越飞越快
so they get going faster and faster

215
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:52,730
越飞越快
and faster and faster...

216
00:11:52,730 --> 00:11:56,440
直到接近光速
And faster until they're almost at the speed of light.

217
00:11:58,510 --> 00:12:01,140
呃，在一个真正的 粒子对撞机中
Well,they're going almost the speed of light

218
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:02,740
它们会几乎达到光速
in a real particle collider,

219
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:06,680
但在这里 它们飞不了那么快
but here they're not going that fast...

220
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,880
飞不了...
[ Straining ] Yet.

221
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,320
[呻吟]
[ Groans ]

222
00:12:12,350 --> 00:12:16,820
这个方向的质子...
So,protons in this direction...

223
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:19,760
与这个方向的质子 互相影响
Interact with protons in this direction,

224
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:21,190
在某个点上
and at some point,

225
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,460
它们像撞车一样撞在一起
they come like a car crashing together.

226
00:12:25,430 --> 00:12:28,400
你能够想像撞车 后发生的事情吧
And you can imagine what happens when a car crashes together.

227
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,640
碎片四溅
Pieces fly all over,

228
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,710
碰撞点四周
and around that interaction point

229
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,510
在那汽车撞倒一起的地方
where the cars crashed together

230
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:37,310
就是我们探测的位置
is where we have our detector.

231
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:42,010
每秒钟里
So,and this happens,

232
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:44,180
这一切会发生 好几百万百万百万次
millions and millions and millions of times every second.

233
00:12:46,490 --> 00:12:49,290
(弗里曼)当你打碎质子
(Freeman) When you break protons apart,

234
00:12:49,290 --> 00:12:52,260
你就释放了难以置信的 巨大能力
you release incredible amounts of energy.

235
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:55,260
爆炸造成了奇怪的事情
Strange things come out of the explosions,

236
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:58,770
在那十亿分之秒中
including tiny particles that flare into existence

237
00:12:58,770 --> 00:13:01,800
各种粒子闪耀出现和消失
and disappear in billionths of a second --

238
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,440
包括反中子
particles like the antineutron

239
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:08,240
以及反质子
and the antimatter version of the proton.

240
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:13,880
理论家们在1920年代就 预告了它们的存在
Theorists had predicted they existed in the 1920s.

241
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:17,720
几十年后，质子加速器 证明了他们的正确
Decades later,the Bevatron proved they were right.

242
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:21,950
突然，我们自认为了解的世界
Suddenly,the world we thought we knew

243
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:25,120
展现了奇怪面貌
got a whole lot stranger.

244
00:13:25,130 --> 00:13:28,060
放射性衰变产生正电子
Positrons from things like radioactive decays

245
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:30,630
正电子来自香蕉或者宇宙射线
like in the banana or cosmic rays

246
00:13:30,630 --> 00:13:33,300
构成了反物质宇宙的半壁
form one half of an antimatter Universe.

247
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:35,700
反质子，来自如同这台机器的设备
Antiprotons from machines like this

248
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:38,700
还有宇宙射线 以及其他自然放射源
and from cosmic rays and other natural sources

249
00:13:38,710 --> 00:13:41,570
构成了反物质宇宙的另一半
form another half of an antimatter Universe.

250
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:42,910
将它们放在一起
Put them together,

251
00:13:42,910 --> 00:13:45,650
你就会得到一个完成的 反物质镜像宇宙
and you've got a complete antimatter mirror Universe

252
00:13:45,650 --> 00:13:47,210
看上去就像是我们的宇宙一样
which just looks like ours

253
00:13:47,210 --> 00:13:50,750
只不过万事都是反打锤 所有东西都是镜像
except everything is backwards,everything is mirrored together.

254
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:54,220
这有点让人吃惊 也许算的上震惊吧
And that's a little bit surprising,shocking maybe,

255
00:13:54,220 --> 00:13:57,120
因为物质宇宙和 反物质宇宙
because matter Universes and antimatter Universes

256
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,490
它们之间相当不和睦
aren't very compatible with each other,

257
00:13:59,490 --> 00:14:01,690
当你把它们放在一起
because when you put them together,

258
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:04,330
只要稍稍接触 它们就湮灭了
when they touch,they annihilate or blow up.

259
00:14:04,330 --> 00:14:06,270
那么，我们究竟 怎么站在这儿的？
So,how did we come to be here?

260
00:14:06,270 --> 00:14:08,800
因为如果在宇宙中存在
Because if there is just as much matter

261
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,670
数量一样的物质和反物质
as antimatter in the Universe,

262
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:13,070
那么一切就如佛曰 色即是空
it should have all combined together

263
00:14:13,070 --> 00:14:15,480
完全空空如也了
and left us with absolutely nothing.

264
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,540
[爆炸]
[ Explosion ]

265
00:14:21,050 --> 00:14:24,520
弗里曼：你在此所见的 微小的光线爆发
(Freeman) The tiny bursts of light you see here

266
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:27,990
是反物质电子 或者说，反电子
are antimatter electrons or positrons.

267
00:14:27,990 --> 00:14:31,220
当它们从这个小小的 放射性碟子逃逸出来
When they leak out of this small radioactive disk,

268
00:14:31,230 --> 00:14:34,390
它们撞上了反电性的电子
they hit the oppositely charged electrons

269
00:14:34,390 --> 00:14:36,660
也就是正常物质的电子
of the normal matter in the chamber

270
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:38,730
于是乎就马上湮灭了
and instantly annihilate,

271
00:14:38,730 --> 00:14:41,730
释放出这些能量的闪光
creating these flashes of energy.

272
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:46,140
正电子和电子是 能够想见的最小粒子
Positrons and electrons are the smallest particles imaginable,

273
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:50,440
所以，能够用凡胎肉眼 看到它们的闪光
so the fact that you can see them explode with the naked eye

274
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:54,480
可以让你想像的出 释放的能量有多么巨大
gives you a hint of how much energy is being released.

275
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:56,820
[急促的哔哔声]
[ Rapid beeping ]

276
00:14:56,820 --> 00:15:00,350
反物质具有极端的高爆性
Antimatter is the ultimate high explosive.

277
00:15:00,350 --> 00:15:03,490
有人担心 使用不当的话
Some worry that,in the wrong hands,

278
00:15:03,490 --> 00:15:07,430
它可能被用来制造 反物质炸弹
it could be used to create an antimatter bomb --

279
00:15:07,430 --> 00:15:09,600
终极超级武器 (oh my ladygaga~~~)
the ultimate super weapon.

280
00:15:12,770 --> 00:15:15,500
(Fajans) 我们不可能 利用反物质
(Fajans) There's no way we're going to destroy the Earth

281
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,670
摧毁我们的地球
using antimatter here.

282
00:15:16,670 --> 00:15:18,440
把一大坨反物质弄到地面上
It's absolutely impossible

283
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:21,370
是完全不可能的事
to get a large amount of antimatter around

284
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:23,780
单单从经济学角度看 也是不着调的事儿
simply on the basis of economics.

285
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:27,680
即使你想制造几克的反物质
If you wanted to make even a couple of grams of antimatter,

286
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:29,950
你也要开动机器
you'd have to run this facility

287
00:15:29,950 --> 00:15:33,220
全力运行上至少几千年
for,in fact,thousands,if not tens of thousands of years

288
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:35,790
那才能产生几克反物质
to make even a few grams of antimatter.

289
00:15:35,790 --> 00:15:38,060
这是基本的物理定律
And this is a fundamental physics issue.

290
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:39,760
这可不是有效率的方式
This isn't an efficiency issue.

291
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:42,630
未来我们能够达到的水平
It's not as if we're going to get much better at this

292
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:44,160
比现在也强不到哪儿去
than we currently are at it.

293
00:15:46,030 --> 00:15:48,600
(弗里曼)欧儿了 你可以放轻松了
(Freeman) So you can relax.

294
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,270
世界很安全
The world is safe.

295
00:15:50,270 --> 00:15:53,510
反物质不是我们的组成部分
Antimatter is what we're not made of.

296
00:15:53,510 --> 00:15:56,480
但是它的确存在
But the fact that it exists at all

297
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:59,880
显露出宇宙实际上是 多么的奇怪
reveals how alien the Universe really is

298
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,920
显露出我们对宇宙力量的 作用方式是多么的无知
and how little we understand the cosmic forces at work

299
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:08,090
显露出我们对自己身体的内部 也了解不多
in the heavens and deep inside our own bodies.

300
00:16:08,090 --> 00:16:09,960
反物质的发现
The discovery of antimatter

301
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:13,090
伴随着对原子内部 更深入的探索
was followed by deeper probing into the heart of the atom

302
00:16:13,090 --> 00:16:15,830
利用更大，更有力的粒子加速器
on larger,more powerful Particle Accelerators.

303
00:16:15,830 --> 00:16:19,400
但是物理学家们 并不喜欢所看到的东西
But physicists didn't like what they saw.

304
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:23,370
观察越深入 看不懂的东西越多
The closer they looked,the less things made sense.

305
00:16:23,370 --> 00:16:25,970
[ Monsters snarling ]

306
00:16:25,970 --> 00:16:27,670
加速器展示出了
The accelerators exposed

307
00:16:27,670 --> 00:16:30,940
一系列令人困惑的神秘粒子
a bewildering array of mysterious particles --

308
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,310
几十种类型
dozens of strains,

309
00:16:32,310 --> 00:16:35,880
小块的物质 看上去各不相同
pieces of matter,all seemingly different.

310
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,120
有些质量难以置信的大
Some were incredibly heavy.

311
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:40,290
有些却根本没有质量
Some had no weight at all.

312
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:46,160
亚原子世界因此得到了 "粒子动物园"的昵称
The subatomic world earned the nickname "The Particle Zoo."

313
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:49,500
(Stanek) 当我们开始研究 粒子动物园中那些
(Stanek) When we were learning about the zoo of particles

314
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:50,900
不知名的粒子
that were not defined,

315
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:54,770
实在是太混沌了 看上去一切都不对劲
it was pretty chaotic,and it just didn't look right.

316
00:16:54,770 --> 00:16:57,000
[ 欢呼 ]
[ Cheering ]

317
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,240
你会想 "这是牛屎
You're thinking,"this is bull crap.

318
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:02,710
应该有比这更强的什么东西"
There's got to be something better than this."

319
00:17:02,710 --> 00:17:04,780
由于这就是全部 你知道
'Cause this is just all,you know,

320
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,980
就像，分类工作 黑魔法
like,just categorizing stuff,black magic,

321
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:10,380
人们都不知道自己在干什么
and people just didn't know what they were doing.

322
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:15,690
(弗里曼)物理学家追求简单
(Freeman) Physics is a quest for simplicity.

323
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:17,160
而这是混沌
This was chaos.

324
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,320
为什么
Why?

325
00:17:18,330 --> 00:17:22,290
为了解开这一谜团 1970年代
To help crack this mystery in the 1970s,

326
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:25,030
合众国建造了Fermilab (费米国家加速器实验室)
the United States built Fermilab,

327
00:17:25,030 --> 00:17:30,140
位于芝加哥郊外30英里的 一个高能研究机构
a high-energy research facility 30 miles outside of Chicago.

328
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:33,940
Fermilab是粒子加速器的巅峰之作
Fermilab sits on top of the Tevatron,

329
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:37,810
4英里长的粒子加速器
a four-mile-long Particle Accelerator.

330
00:17:37,810 --> 00:17:41,650
Leon Lederman 诺贝尔奖得主 试验物理学家
Nobel-prize-winning experimental physicist Leon Lederman

331
00:17:41,650 --> 00:17:44,480
再次完成了很多实验
conducted many of his experiments here.

332
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:48,450
但是，几十年来 他像其他人一样在黑暗中摸索
But for decades,he groped in the dark like everyone else,

333
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:52,290
试图搞明白 这个量子世界的棘手问题
trying to make sense of the messiness of the quantum world.

334
00:17:52,290 --> 00:17:54,030
(Lederman)一点一点的
(Lederman) Little by little,

335
00:17:54,030 --> 00:17:57,730
越来越多的粒子被送进加速器
more and more particles got fed into the hopper

336
00:17:57,730 --> 00:17:59,900
有好几百种粒子
till there were a couple of hundred particles

337
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:02,840
你知道，在1950年代 60年代和70年代
as,you know,in the 1950s,'60s,and '70s,

338
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:06,040
人们开始组织这些粒子
and then people started organizing these particles

339
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,640
给它们编家谱
into family groups,

340
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:10,680
然后，在70年代和80年代早期
and out of this,late '70s,early '80s,

341
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:14,810
完成了名为"标准模型"的 组织形式
came the organization called a Standard Model.

342
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:18,750
但这是逐渐完成的成果
But it was a gradual process,

343
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:20,620
更像是拼图游戏
and it's like a jigsaw puzzle.

344
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:23,490
你拿到了正确一片 把各片逐渐拼在一起
You got the right piece,and everything fell together,

345
00:18:23,490 --> 00:18:26,830
盒子上的画面逐渐成形
and there was the painting on the box cover.

346
00:18:26,830 --> 00:18:30,960
(弗里曼)在研究了上千片 拼图之后
(Freeman) After studying thousands of these jigsaw puzzles,

347
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:34,800
物理学家开始了解 他们看到的究竟是什么
physicists began to understand what they were looking at.

348
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:38,940
Rob Roser负责运行这个 巨大的探测器
Rob Roser runs the giant detector

349
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:42,440
能够为加速器中 物质和反物质碰撞的过程
th takes pictures of matter and antimatter collisions

350
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:44,980
拍下照片
inside the Tevatron.

351
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:48,380
在我身后，是显示CFD探测器中
Behind me is an event display of a proton-antiproton collision

352
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:50,450
质子和反质子碰撞过程的设备
occurring inside the CDF detector.

353
00:18:50,450 --> 00:18:53,250
你可以想象，一个质子 从一个方向出来
You can imagine a proton coming from one direction

354
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:54,650
进入屏幕
in and out of the screen

355
00:18:54,650 --> 00:18:56,760
碰撞中心点
and colliding at the center point.

356
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:59,590
通过观察粒子产生的曲线和曲率
And so by looking at the bend or curvature of the particle,

357
00:18:59,590 --> 00:19:01,090
如果向这个方向弯曲
if it's curved in one direction,

358
00:19:01,090 --> 00:19:02,860
这个粒子就带正电性
that particle's positively charged.

359
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:04,760
如果它向反方向弯曲
If it's bent in an opposite direction,

360
00:19:04,770 --> 00:19:06,600
这个粒子就带负电性
that particle is negatively charged.

361
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:08,700
如果我们划分这个事件
So,if we just break this event down,

362
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:10,800
你可以看到一个单独的 长的，粉红色物体
you can see a single long pink object

363
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,470
指向一个大的 粉红色粒子簇
pointing to a big pink cluster.

364
00:19:12,470 --> 00:19:15,170
颜色越多 粒子具有的能量越多
The more the color,the more energy that particle has.

365
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:17,410
所以你能看到 这是一个单独的粒子
So you can see,here is the single particle

366
00:19:17,410 --> 00:19:18,910
给出了一束能量
that gave up a bunch of energy

367
00:19:18,910 --> 00:19:21,210
就在刻度计的开始部分
right in the initial part of the calorimeter.

368
00:19:21,210 --> 00:19:23,450
表明这是一个电子
That's indicative of an electron.

369
00:19:23,450 --> 00:19:26,120
那里，你看到一条单独的线
Over here,you see a single line

370
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:28,520
那是因为在探测器的后半部 放出了能量
that's giving up energy in the back half of the detector,

371
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:31,520
μ介子一类的物体就会 表现的这样
more characteristic of what a muon object would look like,

372
00:19:31,530 --> 00:19:33,590
μ介子是一种重电子
a muon being a heavy electron.

373
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:36,100
于是，我们通过观察 一些非常简单化的
So we can start to get a lot of information

374
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,060
粒子运行的情况
by just looking at a couple of very simplistic ideas

375
00:19:39,070 --> 00:19:41,470
就可以得到很多信息
in terms of where the particles traveled,

376
00:19:41,470 --> 00:19:42,670
它们偏转的角度
how much they curve,

377
00:19:42,670 --> 00:19:45,440
在探测器的什么部分释放能量
and where they deposited energy in the detector.

378
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,770
弗里曼：今天
(Freeman) Today,

379
00:19:46,770 --> 00:19:50,680
研究了这些亚原子曲线多年之后
after years of reading these subatomic tea leaves,

380
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:53,980
物理学家感觉到
physicists feel they are getting closer

381
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:58,150
他们距离问题答案更近了 问题就是"我们由何构成"
to answering the question,"what are we really made of?"

382
00:19:58,150 --> 00:20:00,450
今天，构成我们的
The stuff that we are made of today

383
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:03,990
也许只是屈指可数的几种粒子
only requires maybe a handful of little particles --

384
00:20:03,990 --> 00:20:07,830
原子外围是电子
the atoms on the outside are electrons

385
00:20:07,830 --> 00:20:11,060
如同行星绕核运行 如果你愿意这样想
whirling around like planets,if you like.

386
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:13,800
原子中心是原子核
There's a nucleus in the middle of the atom

387
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:17,370
我们过去认为 是由质子和中子组成
which we used to believe was made of protons and neutrons.

388
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:20,140
呃，的确是，但是 更近一步，依次的
Well,it is,but deeper down,they,in turn,

389
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:22,940
就像是进入宇宙洋葱的内部
like going to the heart of the cosmic onion,

390
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:25,540
是一些更小的东西 人称"夸克"
are made of little things called quarks.

391
00:20:25,550 --> 00:20:28,980
两只夸克—— 上夸克和下夸克
And two types of quarks -- an up quark and a down quark.

392
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:30,080
And that's it.

393
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,380
上夸克和下夸克
An up and a down quark joined together

394
00:20:32,390 --> 00:20:35,550
通过不同方法结合 最终形成原子核
in different ways ultimately make the atomic nucleus.

395
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:38,790
电子环绕四周，形成原子
An electron whirling around the outside make the atom.

396
00:20:38,790 --> 00:20:40,190
中微子
Throw in a neutrino,

397
00:20:40,190 --> 00:20:43,000
由放射过程产生
which is created in radioactive processes,

398
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,930
它也是组成
and that's the basic particles

399
00:20:44,930 --> 00:20:48,100
你所见万物的粒子之一
that make up everything that you see around you.

400
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:51,040
还有光子
There's also the photon of light,

401
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:54,070
组成了光
which we are seeing with right now,

402
00:20:54,070 --> 00:20:56,310
and that pretty well is it.

403
00:20:56,310 --> 00:20:59,040
(Lederman)我们身体里的 大部分原子
(Lederman) Most of the atoms in our body

404
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:01,450
是由原子核和电子组成
are made of nuclei and electrons,

405
00:21:01,450 --> 00:21:05,350
原子核是由质子和中子组成
and the nuclei themselves are made of protons and neutrons,

406
00:21:05,350 --> 00:21:07,820
质子和中子则由夸克组成
and the protons and neutrons are made of quarks.

407
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:10,990
于是，你自然会问 "夸克是啥子构成的?"
And,of course,you say,"what are the quarks made of?"

408
00:21:10,990 --> 00:21:13,090
这就是我们面对的难题
And that's where we're stuck.

409
00:21:13,090 --> 00:21:16,900
在过去的四、五十年里 我们研究夸克
For the last 40,50 years,we've been studying the quarks,

410
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:18,800
试图从中找出东西来
trying to find something inside,

411
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:21,900
我们得到了在研究电子过程中 相同的结果
and we get the same results we had for the electron.

412
00:21:21,900 --> 00:21:25,200
里头没什么东西 夸克没有尺寸
There's nothing inside. The quarks don't have any size.

413
00:21:25,210 --> 00:21:27,710
夸克的尺寸 夸克的半径是零
The size,the radius of a quark is zero.

414
00:21:27,710 --> 00:21:31,080
这有点像是 "爱丽丝漫游仙境"
It's a little bit like "Alice in Wonderland."

415
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,980
记得爱丽丝看到柴郡猫
Remember when Alice saw the Cheshire cat

416
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:37,780
坐在树枝上 带着大大微笑的样子吗？
sitting on the branch of a tree with a big smile?

417
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:41,850
另爱丽丝非常惊讶的是
And much to Alice's great astonishment,

418
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:43,990
就在她的眼皮底下
right in front of her eyes,

419
00:21:43,990 --> 00:21:46,490
柴郡猫开始消失了
the Cheshire cat started to disappear,

420
00:21:46,490 --> 00:21:50,160
最终—彭！—— 不见了
and finally -- poof! -- It was gone.

421
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:52,830
但还是留下了一部分 它的微笑
But it left behind one component -- its smile.

422
00:21:55,670 --> 00:22:00,910
弗里曼：夸克的微笑 是一个塞满了能量的盒子
(Freeman) That quark smile is a tiny box stuffed full of energy.

423
00:22:00,910 --> 00:22:04,280
所有物质实际上 是由能量产生的
All matter is actually made of energy

424
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:07,910
是凝结成粒子形态的能量
that has congealed into particulate form.

425
00:22:07,910 --> 00:22:11,780
所以，看起来 我们是由能量构成——
So that appears to be what we are made of --

426
00:22:11,790 --> 00:22:15,350
至少就目前的情况看是这样
at least as far as we can see right now.

427
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:18,620
但是，了解到这些之后 另一个谜题出现了
But knowing this opens up an even greater mystery,

428
00:22:18,630 --> 00:22:22,530
那就是—为什么构成我们的 这些材料
which is -- why does the stuff we are made of

429
00:22:22,530 --> 00:22:25,400
以眼下的形式运行?
behave the way it does?

430
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:27,030
我们对物质的探索
Our explorations of matter

431
00:22:27,030 --> 00:22:30,170
显示出所有的物体 是几乎空心的
reveal that everything is nearly hollow --

432
00:22:30,170 --> 00:22:33,240
你，我，宇宙中的万物
you,me,and everything in the Universe.

433
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:36,510
都是大量的空间 和一些小小的
It's all an empty space with a few pinpricks of matter

434
00:22:36,510 --> 00:22:41,110
飘浮在空虚中的物质 就像无尽空间中漂泊的石头
floating in a void like rocks adrift in the vastness of space.

435
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:43,920
但是，这些飘浮的物质
But how do these pinpricks of matter

436
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:46,750
是怎样构成外形和结构？
form into shapes and structures?

437
00:22:46,750 --> 00:22:49,690
一定有种力量 将它聚在一起
There must be something holding it together --

438
00:22:49,690 --> 00:22:53,490
空虚海洋中的一种粘合物
some sort of glue in the ocean of emptiness.

439
00:22:53,490 --> 00:22:56,960
问题是，是啥?
The question is,what?

440
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:11,000
弗里曼：今天，我们认为 我们知道自己是由何构成
(Freeman) Today,we think we know what we're made out of --

441
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,170
难以置信的小建材
the incredibly small building blocks

442
00:23:13,170 --> 00:23:15,700
构成了宇宙中的所有物质
that form all the matter in the Universe.

443
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:18,670
但是，随着找到这些小块物质
But finding these bits and pieces of matter

444
00:23:18,670 --> 00:23:22,210
另一个更具挑战性的 神秘问题出现了
revealed another even more challenging mystery --

445
00:23:22,210 --> 00:23:24,780
物体为什么是实心的？
why are things solid?

446
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:28,580
为什么他们有体积?
Why do they have mass?

447
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:30,520
物质几乎是完全的空间
Matter is mostly eupty space.

448
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:33,850
不时的，你在某点 发现一个原子
Every now and then,you find the point of an atom,

449
00:23:33,860 --> 00:23:36,560
但是大多数时间 这点上是空的
but most of the time,it's empty space.

450
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:40,490
所以，这个原子和那个原子
So,that point of atom and that point of atom and so on --

451
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:42,230
它们如何组合在一起？
how are they held together?

452
00:23:42,230 --> 00:23:44,600
你是怎样组合起来的？ 我是怎样组合起来的？
How are you held together? How am I held together?

453
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:48,500
可不是靠胶水 你知道，不是胶水
It's not glue. You know it's not glue.

454
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:52,140
应该有某种基本属性的交换
It has to be some exchange of fundamental properties.

455
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:54,010
某种力的交换
That exchange of forces has to happen --

456
00:23:54,010 --> 00:23:55,380
即使目不可见
even though you don't see it --

457
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:58,580
这种力也在世界范围内 各个角落发生着作用
has to happen at the global level everywhere.

458
00:23:58,580 --> 00:24:01,450
(弗里曼)空间实际上并不空
(Freeman) Empty space isn't empty at all.

459
00:24:01,450 --> 00:24:03,320
空间充满了力
It's filled with forces.

460
00:24:03,320 --> 00:24:07,150
当这些人把球 扔来扔去
When these men toss this basketball back and forth,

461
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,860
他们在传递球的动量
they're transferring the momentum of the ball

462
00:24:09,860 --> 00:24:13,790
从一个传给另一个 将他们分离开
from one to the other,which pushes them apart --

463
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:17,400
彼此间不可见力量的
a complex exchange of invisible forces

464
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,270
复杂传递
talking to each other.

465
00:24:20,270 --> 00:24:21,970
有四种基本的作用力
So,there are four fundamental forces --

466
00:24:21,970 --> 00:24:24,040
引力 所有人都知道
the gravitation force that everybody knows about,

467
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:26,570
电磁力 几乎所有人都知道
the electromagnetic force,which mostly everybody knows about,

468
00:24:26,570 --> 00:24:28,410
弱相互作用 你不知道的东西
the weak force,which you don't know about,

469
00:24:28,410 --> 00:24:30,480
还有强相互作用 你还是不知道的东西
and the strong force,which you don't know about.

470
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:35,580
弱相互作用 决定了放射性衰变
The weak force is what determines radioactive decay.

471
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:39,150
铀衰变成为何物
How uranium decays into whatever it decays into --

472
00:24:39,150 --> 00:24:41,260
这就是由弱相互作用控制的
that's governed by the weak forces.

473
00:24:41,260 --> 00:24:44,990
强相互作用 将质子组合在一起
The strong forces are what holds the proton together,

474
00:24:44,990 --> 00:24:48,730
强相互作用把3个夸克 组成一个质子
what holds the quarks into three pieces that form a proton.

475
00:24:48,730 --> 00:24:51,670
我们这些家伙已经明白了 强相互作用和弱相互作用
So,us guys are doing the weak forces and the strong forces,

476
00:24:51,670 --> 00:24:54,470
但我们对引力还不是很了解
and what we don't understand is the gravitational force,

477
00:24:54,470 --> 00:24:57,100
我们认为自己 已经了解了电磁作用
and we think we understand the electromagnetic force.

478
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:02,340
弗里曼：因为我们不能看到 那些组成我们的基本粒子
(Freeman) Just as we can't see the things we're made of,

479
00:25:02,340 --> 00:25:05,110
我们也无法看到 环绕身边的基本作用
we can't see the fundamental forces around us.

480
00:25:05,110 --> 00:25:07,980
但我们知道 它们就在那里
But we know they're there.

481
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:09,980
找出这些作用的工作原理
Finding out how these forces work

482
00:25:09,980 --> 00:25:12,520
以及它们的本源
and where they came from in the first place

483
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:15,620
正是现代物理学的 主要探索目标
is the great quest of modern physics.

484
00:25:15,620 --> 00:25:17,620
解决了这些谜团
Solving this mystery

485
00:25:17,630 --> 00:25:21,660
可以解开宇宙最深处的秘密
could reveal the Universe's most closely held secrets --

486
00:25:21,660 --> 00:25:23,930
不仅是我们由何组成
not just what we're made of,

487
00:25:23,930 --> 00:25:27,600
还有体内的众多粒子 组合起来的原因
but why the stuff inside us holds its shape.

488
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:30,540
粒子物理学的关键突破
The key breakthrough in particle physics

489
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:31,840
在于发现了
was the discovery

490
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:35,440
某种粒子实际上是 作用力的携带者
that certain particles are actually force carriers.

491
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:38,750
举例来讲，光子— 组成光的粒子—
For instance,photons -- particles of light --

492
00:25:38,750 --> 00:25:40,980
携带了电磁作用
carry the electromagnetic force.

493
00:25:40,980 --> 00:25:43,420
所有的作用都有 对应的携带者
All the forces have these carriers.

494
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:45,390
虽然我们还没找到 所有的携带者
We haven't found them all yet,

495
00:25:45,390 --> 00:25:48,390
但我们已经能够确定 它们的存在
but we've found enough to know they're there.

496
00:25:48,390 --> 00:25:51,390
我们知道它们是如何影响的
And we know enough about how they interact

497
00:25:51,390 --> 00:25:54,800
我们意识到 在极高的温度下
to realize that at extremely high temperatures --

498
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:56,930
大概几千亿度的高温
around a million,billion degrees --

499
00:25:56,930 --> 00:26:00,430
电磁作用和弱相互作用 开始融合
the electromagnetic and the weak force begin to merge.

500
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:04,370
这种融合被称为 电弱统一
This merging is called electroweak unification.

501
00:26:04,370 --> 00:26:08,380
你不必非要理解它 —我当然也不—
You don't have to understand it -- I certainly don't --

502
00:26:08,380 --> 00:26:12,310
但对物理学家来说 这就像是找到失落的联系
but to physicists,it was like finding the missing link.

503
00:26:15,350 --> 00:26:19,250
这种关系指出了 通向科学史上
It led the way to one of the most successful theories

504
00:26:19,250 --> 00:26:21,360
最为成功理论之一的道路—
in the history of science --

505
00:26:21,360 --> 00:26:24,830
这一理论就是 粒子物理学的标准模型
the Standard Model of particle physics.

506
00:26:24,830 --> 00:26:27,890
在过去的40年间 它的正确性已经被
It's been proving correct again and again

507
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:30,430
一次又一次的证明
over the last 40 years.

508
00:26:30,430 --> 00:26:34,570
但标准模型有一个问题
But there is a problem with the Standard Model --

509
00:26:34,570 --> 00:26:35,970
一个大问题
A big problem.

510
00:26:35,970 --> 00:26:40,810
回到粒子动物园
And it goes back to The Particle Zoo --

511
00:26:40,810 --> 00:26:44,910
当你碰撞质子 看看里面有什么时
strange particles that turn up when you smash together protons

512
00:26:44,910 --> 00:26:47,310
奇怪的粒子出现了
to see what's inside.

513
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:53,250
亚原子粒子的重量 或者说质量差异巨大
Subatomic particles have a huge range of weight,or mass.

514
00:26:53,250 --> 00:26:54,420
例如
For instance,

515
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:57,890
一个空点夸克的质量
one point-blank quark can weigh 200 times more

516
00:26:57,890 --> 00:27:00,130
是电子的200多倍
than the point-blank electron,

517
00:27:00,130 --> 00:27:02,900
而这些粒子 甚至还有质量更大的表亲
and these particles have even heavier cousins

518
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:05,670
质量达到十万倍
weighing 100,000 times more.

519
00:27:05,670 --> 00:27:08,540
标准模型无法解释
The Standard Model cannot explain

520
00:27:08,540 --> 00:27:11,910
质量分布范围为何如此之广
why there is such a wild range of masses

521
00:27:11,910 --> 00:27:15,480
甚至无法解释 粒子为什么具有质量
or even why particles have any mass at all.

522
00:27:17,610 --> 00:27:19,510
解决这个问题
Fixing this problem

523
00:27:19,510 --> 00:27:23,020
成为现代物理学家 有待解决的下一个问题
became the next great quest of modern physics.

524
00:27:23,020 --> 00:27:28,360
拯救来自于这个 看上去不太像有这种本事的男人
Salvation came in the unlikely form of this man.

525
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:30,390
有请Peter Higgs
Meet Peter Higgs,

526
00:27:30,390 --> 00:27:34,430
一位低调的教授 他领导了科学史上
an unassuming Professor who set off one of the largest

527
00:27:34,430 --> 00:27:36,800
最巨大、最昂贵的
and most expensive investigations

528
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:38,530
研究活动之一
in the history of science.

529
00:27:38,530 --> 00:27:42,570
在标准模型的宇宙中 有一个缺陷
There was a gapping hole in the Standard Model of the Universe.

530
00:27:42,570 --> 00:27:45,870
Peter Higgs填补了它
Peter Higgs put a plug in it.

531
00:27:47,310 --> 00:27:49,810
Higgs提出了这样的理论
Higgs theorized that a vast field

532
00:27:49,810 --> 00:27:53,180
拉伸至无限的巨大空间域 贯穿万物
stretching to infinity runs through everything.

533
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:56,580
当某种粒子与这个域发生交互
When certain kinds of particles interact with the field,

534
00:27:56,580 --> 00:28:00,720
这种交互就赋予粒子质量
that interaction is what gives those particles mass.

535
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:04,020
如果Higgs的理论成真
If Higgs' theory becomes fact,

536
00:28:04,030 --> 00:28:09,300
我们可以最终解释 为什么物体的实在性
we may finally understand why things are solid.

537
00:28:09,300 --> 00:28:14,430
但是首先，Higgs在让人 接受他的理论时遇到了困难
But at first,Higgs had trouble getting his theory accepted.

538
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:18,670
一篇相关的论文 被CERN拒绝了
A paper outlining the idea was rejected by CERN.

539
00:28:18,670 --> 00:28:20,710
(Higgs) [ 英式口音 ] 偶怒了
(Higgs) [ british accent ] I was indignant,

540
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:22,110
我认为我所做的事情
because I thought what I'd done

541
00:28:22,110 --> 00:28:23,910
具有重大的意义
had possibly important consequences.

542
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:28,450
所以我重写了论文 加了几段重要的内容
So I rewrote the paper by adding on some extra paragraphs,

543
00:28:28,450 --> 00:28:30,750
我没再把论文寄到日内瓦
and instead of sending it back to Geneva,

544
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:33,450
CERN的人太逊了 他们听不懂
where I thought the people at CERN didn't understand

545
00:28:33,450 --> 00:28:34,920
俺的高深理论
what I was talking about,

546
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:38,430
我把论文寄给了大西洋彼岸 Physical Review Letters期刊
I sent it across the Atlantic to Physical Review Letters,

547
00:28:38,430 --> 00:28:40,960
学术地位相当的美国期刊
the corresponding American journal,

548
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:42,760
论文被接受了
and it was accepted.

549
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:44,760
(弗里曼)Higgs增加的段落
(Freeman) The paragraphs Higgs added

550
00:28:44,770 --> 00:28:46,970
预言说赋予质量的域
predicted that the mass-giving field

551
00:28:46,970 --> 00:28:49,170
会有对应的粒子
would have a matching particle,

552
00:28:49,170 --> 00:28:52,440
一种称作Higgs玻色子的 作用携带者
a force carrier called a Higgs Boson.

553
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,610
这种粒子
And this matching particle

554
00:28:54,610 --> 00:28:59,180
理论上能够在粒子加速器中 被制造出来
could theoretically be created in a Particle Accelerator.

555
00:28:59,180 --> 00:29:00,550
渐渐的
Gradually,

556
00:29:00,550 --> 00:29:05,120
试验物理学家 对Higgs的主意感到激动
experimental physicists became excited by Higgs' idea.

557
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:07,820
(Lederman) 当然，现在一小部分
(Lederman) What happens with a theory is,of course,

558
00:29:07,820 --> 00:29:10,090
理论家们接受了这个理论
a small number of theorists push this idea.

559
00:29:10,090 --> 00:29:11,120
他们爱这个理论
They love it.

560
00:29:11,130 --> 00:29:12,360
而且渐渐的
And little by little,

561
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:15,060
更多的理论家上了这条船 你知道吗？
more and more theorists climb on board,you know?

562
00:29:15,060 --> 00:29:17,030
像一趟火车 "呜呜!"
It's like the train. "Whoo Whoo!"

563
00:29:17,030 --> 00:29:19,370
我们上路了 我们离开了站台
We're gone,and we're taking off from the station.

564
00:29:19,370 --> 00:29:24,300
弗里曼：现代科学 最具反讽意味的事情之一
(Freeman) In one of the great ironies of modern science,

565
00:29:24,310 --> 00:29:28,010
CERN，拒绝了Higgs论文的 研究机构
CERN,the organization that rejected Higgs' paper,

566
00:29:28,010 --> 00:29:31,240
刚刚投入100亿美元
has just spent $10 billion

567
00:29:31,250 --> 00:29:35,480
建造新的设备 寻找Higgs粒子.
building a machine to find the Higgs particle.

568
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:40,120
但是Higgs理论 究竟是啥玩意？
But what exactly is the Higgs?

569
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:41,620
问几个物理学家
Ask a half dozen physicists,

570
00:29:41,620 --> 00:29:44,160
你就会得到几种不同的答案
and you'll get a half dozen different answers.

571
00:29:44,160 --> 00:29:46,190
[ 英式口音 ] Higgs理论
[ British accent ] The Higgs.

572
00:29:46,190 --> 00:29:47,330
是一种微妙的东西
It's a tricky thing

573
00:29:47,330 --> 00:29:49,260
像Higgs玻色子
to come up with an analogy for Higgs Bosons.

574
00:29:49,260 --> 00:29:50,760
它是
It's --

575
00:29:50,770 --> 00:29:52,600
有点像
there's the analogy

576
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:54,900
从糖浆里拉过什么东西
with something being dragged through treacle,

577
00:29:54,900 --> 00:29:56,940
但对我来说 这是误导
but for me,that's misleading,

578
00:29:56,940 --> 00:29:59,310
因为这是浪费能量
because this is a dissipation of energy,

579
00:29:59,310 --> 00:30:00,440
它并不像那样
and it isn't like that.

580
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:03,540
那是关于Higgs粒子的 不怎么样的比喻
That's a pretty bad analogy for the Higgs.

581
00:30:03,540 --> 00:30:07,010
我所了解的Higgs粒子 在我的脑海中，它是非常混乱的
What I've read on the Higgs is,in my mind,very confusing.

582
00:30:07,010 --> 00:30:09,780
[ 笑 ]
[ Laughs ]

583
00:30:09,780 --> 00:30:11,320
这就是我的理解
Here's the way I understand it.

584
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:15,220
一群记者站在屋子里 拥挤的屋子
A bunch of reporters standing in a room,crowded room.

585
00:30:15,220 --> 00:30:17,090
我和小奥总统也在
And so me and President Obama

586
00:30:17,090 --> 00:30:20,060
试图从房间入口
want to make it from the entrance of this room

587
00:30:20,060 --> 00:30:21,760
挤到出口去
to the exit of this room.

588
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:23,730
我们进来了，会发生什么？
So we go in,and what happens?

589
00:30:23,730 --> 00:30:26,870
当然，所有的记者 涌向奥巴马
Of course,all the reporters glom on Mr. Obama.

590
00:30:26,870 --> 00:30:28,230
还有老Bob
And old Bob over here,

591
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:31,040
他于是努力直奔下个门而去
he just makes a beeline right to the exit door.

592
00:30:31,040 --> 00:30:34,770
当然，基本上，努力的话 我会到达那个门
So,basically,with no inertia,I can make it to that door,

593
00:30:34,780 --> 00:30:38,210
但是奥巴马的难度更大 更大的质量
whereas Mr. Obama has a lot of inertia,a lot of mass.

594
00:30:38,210 --> 00:30:41,410
所以Higgs域对不同粒子的
So this Higgs field affects one particle

595
00:30:41,420 --> 00:30:43,650
影响作用不同
more so than another particle.

596
00:30:43,650 --> 00:30:45,650
[英式口音]必须找到
[ British accent ] Must be able to come up with a more --

597
00:30:45,650 --> 00:30:47,890
呃，当我们研究 它们看上去像什么的时候
well,when we see what they look like,

598
00:30:47,890 --> 00:30:49,720
我们会找到一种 更好的比拟方式
we'll come up with a better analogy.

599
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:51,420
另一种比拟，欧耶
Another analogy,yeah.

600
00:30:51,430 --> 00:30:54,190
包括汽车或其它东西
Something involving cars or something.

601
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:55,630
[ 笑] 我不知道
[ Laughing ] I don't know.

602
00:30:55,630 --> 00:30:58,830
(弗里曼)无论你怎么描述
(Freeman) However you describe it,

603
00:30:58,830 --> 00:31:02,240
Higgs理论解决了 来自粒子动物园的
the Higgs solves a slew of problems,

604
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:04,800
大量问题
starting with The Particle Zoo.

605
00:31:06,110 --> 00:31:08,880
这是个很优雅的主意 如果你接受它
It's a very elegant idea,because if you accept it,

606
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:11,710
我们关于粒子的图景 一下子简单了
then our whole picture of particles becomes simpler.

607
00:31:11,710 --> 00:31:13,410
没有那么多的粒子
There are not so many particles.

608
00:31:13,410 --> 00:31:16,780
是质量因素造成 看上去有那么多的粒子
It's the mass that makes it look as if there are many particles.

609
00:31:16,780 --> 00:31:18,720
有点像万花筒
A little bit like a kaleidoscope,

610
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:20,590
当你看着里面的多面镜子
where you look in with a lot of mirrors,

611
00:31:20,590 --> 00:31:22,520
实际上只有一定的模式
and there's only one little pattern,

612
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:24,960
但是因为在镜子间反射又反射
but it's reflected and reflected in mirrors,

613
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:27,060
看上去就复杂多了
and it looks very complicated.

614
00:31:27,060 --> 00:31:30,230
Higgs现象是简化标准模型的
The Higgs phenomenon is a very satisfying way

615
00:31:30,230 --> 00:31:32,770
一个非常令人满意的理论
of simplifying our Standard Model.

616
00:31:32,770 --> 00:31:37,270
弗里曼：Higgs理论赋予 基本的物质种子以质量
(Freeman) The Higgs gives mass to the basic seeds of matter,

617
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:41,910
像电子、原子和质子里的夸克
such as the electron and atoms and the quarks inside protons.

618
00:31:41,910 --> 00:31:44,380
因为电子的质量
Because the mass of the electron

619
00:31:44,380 --> 00:31:46,910
有助于决定原子的大小
helps determine the size of the atom,

620
00:31:46,910 --> 00:31:51,790
Higgs理论给出了我们所知 各种东西的结构和形式
the Higgs gives structure and form to everything we know.

621
00:31:52,790 --> 00:31:54,990
如果你关掉它
If you turned it off,

622
00:31:54,990 --> 00:31:58,530
你，我，你的狗 这个行星
you,me,your dog,and the planet

623
00:31:58,530 --> 00:32:01,360
都会以光速飞散
would fly apart at the speed of light.

624
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:03,630
玻璃破碎
[ Glass shatters ]

625
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:06,130
你如何发现一种
So,how do you find an invisible,

626
00:32:06,130 --> 00:32:09,000
不可见，甚至不可探测的自然作用力？
seemingly undetectable force of nature?

627
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:12,710
所有的作用都有相关的粒子 我们可以看到这些粒子
All the forces have related particles that we can see,

628
00:32:12,710 --> 00:32:14,170
只要有足够的能量
given enough energy.

629
00:32:14,180 --> 00:32:15,640
利用正确的工具
With the right tool,

630
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:18,280
我们可以创造这些作用粒子
we can create those force particles,

631
00:32:18,280 --> 00:32:20,050
尽管人们后来才发现
although as it turns out,

632
00:32:20,050 --> 00:32:23,150
开发一种能够 检测到Higgs粒子的工具
it's taken nearly 50 years to develop a tool

633
00:32:23,150 --> 00:32:24,850
花费了大概50年光阴
that may spot the Higgs.

634
00:32:29,790 --> 00:32:33,430
这是欧洲核子研究中心的大型强子对撞机
This is CERN's Large Hadron Collider.

635
00:32:33,430 --> 00:32:38,600
开满功率，它能达到 7万亿电子伏特
At full power,it can channel 7 trillion electron volts,

636
00:32:38,600 --> 00:32:40,170
它是史上最强的
making it by far

637
00:32:40,170 --> 00:32:44,600
高能粒子加速器
the highest energy particle accelerator ever made.

638
00:32:44,610 --> 00:32:49,140
LHC的能量越大 碰撞威力也越大
The higher energy levels of the LHC produced bigger collisions

639
00:32:49,140 --> 00:32:52,010
也迸出越多的粒子
that spurt out more massive particles.

640
00:32:52,010 --> 00:32:53,550
这提高了发现概率
This raises the odds

641
00:32:53,550 --> 00:32:56,920
每秒钟有数十亿次碰撞
that out of the billions of collisions produced each second,

642
00:32:56,920 --> 00:33:01,790
LHC会发现人类从未见的现象
the LHC will find things humans have never seen before --

643
00:33:01,790 --> 00:33:04,990
比如Higgs粒子
things like the Higgs.

644
00:33:04,990 --> 00:33:09,560
但是LHC的本事可不止 在于寻找微小的粒子
But the LHC will do much more than find a tiny particle,

645
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:12,730
他们在CERN建造的设备
because what they've really built at CERN

646
00:33:12,730 --> 00:33:14,970
实际上是一个大爆炸机器
is a Big-Bang machine.

647
00:33:14,970 --> 00:33:18,340
当试图解决物质谜题的时候
While trying to solve the mystery of matter,

648
00:33:18,340 --> 00:33:21,110
物理学家意识到
physicists realized that they're on the trail

649
00:33:21,110 --> 00:33:25,980
他们在追踪一个更大的谜题-也许是终极谜题
of a much bigger mystery -- perhaps the ultimate mystery.

650
00:33:25,980 --> 00:33:30,720
在创世之初究竟发生了什么？
What happened in the first moments of creation?

651
00:33:30,720 --> 00:33:32,890
[ 爆炸 ]
[ Explosion ]

652
00:33:42,050 --> 00:33:43,480
弗里曼：现在
(Freeman) Right now,

653
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:47,320
数千名科学侦探 在搜寻Higgs玻色子
thousands of science detectives hunt the Higgs Boson --

654
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:50,660
难以捉摸的粒子 赋予万物以质量
the elusive particle that gives everything mass,

655
00:33:50,660 --> 00:33:54,700
把物质粘合成形
the thing that may keep matter glued together.

656
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:58,800
他们试图解决的谜团 要比开始时所想象的
The mystery they are trying to solve is much,much bigger

657
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:00,800
大的多的多
than anyone first imagined.

658
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:02,840
为了解决它
To solve it,

659
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:05,670
他们必须回到
they have to go back to the beginning

660
00:34:05,670 --> 00:34:09,140
宇宙创世之初
and re-create the first moments of the Universe.

661
00:34:10,740 --> 00:34:15,580
就在大爆炸刚发生之后
In the first moments just after the big bang happened,

662
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:17,580
难以置信的炎热
it was incredibly hot --

663
00:34:17,580 --> 00:34:21,620
万亿亿度的高温.
billions of billions of degrees.

664
00:34:21,620 --> 00:34:23,960
热量就是能量
And heat is energy.

665
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:27,460
而能量凝结成物质形式
And the energy congealed into forms of matter,

666
00:34:27,460 --> 00:34:29,660
其中许多种 我们已经解开了
many of which we have already discovered,

667
00:34:29,660 --> 00:34:33,000
我们只需相信
many of which we only believe exist

668
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:35,400
因为我们的公式已经证明了
because of our equations.

669
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:37,670
其中的大多数
Most of these things only lived

670
00:34:37,670 --> 00:34:40,140
只存在几百亿分之一秒
for a trillionth of a second themself.

671
00:34:40,140 --> 00:34:42,170
它们被创造，又死去
They were made,they died away

672
00:34:42,180 --> 00:34:46,380
但是留下了儿子，孙子 等等
and left children,grandchildren,and so forth.

673
00:34:46,380 --> 00:34:48,610
稳定物质中
This cascading down

674
00:34:48,620 --> 00:34:50,520
这种短命粒子的级联效应
from these ephemeral particles

675
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:53,520
发生的非常快
into the stable stuff took place very quickly.

676
00:34:53,520 --> 00:34:56,190
稳定物质最终凝结成为
The stable stuff then ends up congealing

677
00:34:56,190 --> 00:35:00,090
今天组成你和我的各种物质
to make the stuff that you and I and everybody's made of today.

678
00:35:00,090 --> 00:35:01,630
我们所作的
So,what we're doing

679
00:35:01,630 --> 00:35:06,200
就是在实验室中 重现宇宙创始的时刻
is re-creating in the lab the first moments of the Universe,

680
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:09,570
环绕着碰撞位置
and then by surrounding the site of the collisions

681
00:35:09,570 --> 00:35:12,140
布置了特别的相机，探测器
with these special cameras,detectors,

682
00:35:12,140 --> 00:35:14,510
我们可以记录发生了什么事
we can record what happened.

683
00:35:14,510 --> 00:35:18,280
我们正在模拟大爆炸后的情形
And so we are simulating just after the big bang,

684
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:21,610
制造迷你大爆炸 如果你愿意，在实验室里
making mini bangs,if you like,in the lab.

685
00:35:21,620 --> 00:35:23,650
通过研究成果
And from what we find there,

686
00:35:23,650 --> 00:35:27,020
在150亿年之后
we begin to get a sense of how matter,

687
00:35:27,020 --> 00:35:30,060
我们开始对物质的组成
the stuff that we ultimately,15 billion years later,

688
00:35:30,060 --> 00:35:32,690
开始有了概念
are made of,first came to be.

689
00:35:32,690 --> 00:35:36,260
弗里曼：Jon Butterworth 是一个物理学家
(Freeman) Jon Butterworth is a physicist

690
00:35:36,260 --> 00:35:39,600
供职于伦敦大学学院
at the University College of London.

691
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:43,170
Adam Davison是一个博士后
Adam Davison is a postdoctoral student.

692
00:35:43,170 --> 00:35:45,670
他们是在CERN做研究的
They're two of the 6,000 scientists

693
00:35:45,670 --> 00:35:48,240
六千名科学家中的两位
conducting experiments back at CERN,

694
00:35:48,240 --> 00:35:52,680
CERN，欧洲原子能研究机构
the European organization for nuclear research.

695
00:35:54,450 --> 00:35:57,350
CERN本身— 是的，并不是非常可爱
CERN itself is quite -- yeah,is not terribly pretty.

696
00:35:57,350 --> 00:36:00,150
它看上去像是某人在地面上 倾倒了一堆锈迹斑斑的砖块
It looks like someone dropped a load of rusty bricks on the ground.

697
00:36:00,150 --> 00:36:01,790
我对CERN缺乏建筑计划的作风
I get the impression that there was never much

698
00:36:01,790 --> 00:36:03,090
印象深刻
of an architectural plan for CERN.

699
00:36:03,090 --> 00:36:04,720
但当你深入地下，当然
Until you go underground,of course,

700
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:07,290
它看上去像是007敌人的什么设施
and then it's like something out of a James Bond villain set.

701
00:36:07,290 --> 00:36:09,500
[ 笑 ]
[ Laughs ]

702
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:14,500
这些，作为工程成果 是一个奇迹
This,as a piece of engineering,is a miracle.

703
00:36:14,500 --> 00:36:16,700
这是我们时代的金字塔
It is the pyramids of our time.

704
00:36:19,870 --> 00:36:23,680
(弗里曼)CERN的核心 是巨强子对撞机
(Freeman) The heart of CERN is the Large Hadron Collider,

705
00:36:23,680 --> 00:36:27,710
价值百亿美元，17英里长的 粒子加速器
a $10 billion,17-mile-long Particle Accelerator.

706
00:36:27,710 --> 00:36:31,450
这也许是有史以来
It is quite possibly the most sophisticated

707
00:36:31,450 --> 00:36:34,490
最为精致的科学实验设备
scientific instrument ever built.

708
00:36:34,490 --> 00:36:37,190
[ 爆炸]
[ Explosion ]

709
00:36:37,190 --> 00:36:41,690
LHC创造了最原始的爆炸
The LHC creates the primordial explosions,

710
00:36:41,700 --> 00:36:46,870
沿着加速器布置的 四个巨大探测器
then four enormous detectors along the accelerator ring

711
00:36:46,870 --> 00:36:49,030
拍下了碰撞的过程
take pictures of the collisions.

712
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:54,710
两个最大的探测器叫做 Atlas和CMS
The two largest detectors are called Atlas and CMS.

713
00:36:54,710 --> 00:36:57,480
麻省理工的Steve Nahn 领导着一个小组
M.I.T.'S Steve Nahn leads a team

714
00:36:57,480 --> 00:37:01,850
帮助设计和运行CMS探测器
that helped design and now runs the CMS detector.

715
00:37:01,850 --> 00:37:05,250
(Nahn) 我们建造的探测器
(Nahn) We build our detectors to take pictures of the events

716
00:37:05,250 --> 00:37:07,320
能够记录每25纳秒发生一次的事件
which happen once every 25 nanoseconds.

717
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:09,660
也就是每秒钟4千万次
That's 40 million times a second

718
00:37:09,660 --> 00:37:13,290
我们有一个想要记录的 交互作用
we have an interaction that we want to take a picture of.

719
00:37:13,500 --> 00:37:17,470
硬盘记录了1T又1T的数据
So,with this terabytes and terabytes of data on disk,

720
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:19,370
我们必须编写程序
we have to write algorithms

721
00:37:19,370 --> 00:37:22,210
来筛选和寻找研究对象
which sift through and find that event,

722
00:37:22,210 --> 00:37:24,510
千万里挑一 亿里挑一
that one in 10 million,one in 100 million,

723
00:37:24,510 --> 00:37:26,980
十亿里挑一
one in a billion event that you're looking for.

724
00:37:31,650 --> 00:37:34,350
(弗里曼)在LHC的另一端
(Freeman) On the other side of the LHC,

725
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:36,520
Butterworth和Davison 开发了一种方法
Butterworth and Davison have developed a way

726
00:37:36,520 --> 00:37:38,790
从CMS产生的海量的数据中
to comb through the enormous amounts of data

727
00:37:38,790 --> 00:37:43,760
挑选出所需内容
generated by CMS's archrival,the Atlas detector.

728
00:37:43,770 --> 00:37:46,330
这两个人试图绘制
The two men are trying to create maps

729
00:37:46,330 --> 00:37:49,140
描述亚原子世界
of what they think the subatomic Universe looked like

730
00:37:49,140 --> 00:37:51,370
创造出来一秒钟之后情况的地图
just seconds after its creation,

731
00:37:51,370 --> 00:37:55,140
然后与实际情况对照
then matching their imaginary maps up to reality.

732
00:37:55,140 --> 00:38:00,110
通过这样的方法 他们希望能找到Higgs粒子
Somewhere in there,they hope they'll find the Higgs.

733
00:38:00,110 --> 00:38:02,420
就像是环绕 某个不知名乡村的边界
It's kind of like a border around an unknown country.

734
00:38:02,420 --> 00:38:03,780
我们知道它就在那儿
And we know that it's there.

735
00:38:03,790 --> 00:38:06,250
我们已经进行了 能量足够大的实验
We've had experiments that have gone to high enough energy

736
00:38:06,250 --> 00:38:08,760
实验证明具有边界 以及超越边界的领地
to tell us there is a border and there is a land beyond it,

737
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:11,290
但我们还不能看到那片土地
but we've not had really much of a glimpse of the land.

738
00:38:11,290 --> 00:38:15,100
LHC将使我们穿过边界
So,the LHC really is gonna let us over that border

739
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:17,630
让我们看到那片土地 测量它，观察它
and let us have a look at this land and survey it and see.

740
00:38:17,630 --> 00:38:19,500
这就是为什么 当人们问道
And this is why people,when people ask,

741
00:38:19,500 --> 00:38:21,030
你知道 我们会找到什么
you know,what we're gonna find,

742
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,970
"你什么时候会的诺贝尔奖？"
"when are you gonna get your nobel prize?"

743
00:38:22,970 --> 00:38:24,170
我们不知道
We just don't know.

744
00:38:24,170 --> 00:38:26,240
我们知道的是 如果Higgs粒子存在
We know that if the Higgs exists,

745
00:38:26,240 --> 00:38:28,480
它会在边界的那边
it will be in that country somewhere,

746
00:38:28,480 --> 00:38:30,040
而我们的设备足够好 有能力发现它
and our kit is good enough to find it.

747
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:31,880
也许需要几年时间 但是我们能找到它
It might take a few years,but we'll find it.

748
00:38:35,050 --> 00:38:40,150
回到美国 费米实验室并未放弃
Meanwhile,back in America,Fermilab hasn't given up.

749
00:38:40,150 --> 00:38:43,190
这是一场找寻Higgs粒子的竞赛
It's a race against the clock to find the Higgs

750
00:38:43,190 --> 00:38:46,060
在CERN的LHC运行之前
before CERN's LHC powers up.

751
00:38:46,060 --> 00:38:48,460
当然 我们在芝加哥
Of course,we're here in Chicago,

752
00:38:48,460 --> 00:38:51,600
我们很希望在芝加哥 有这样的设备
and we'd love to have that machine in Chicago.

753
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:55,070
所以我们看着 欧洲同行的成功
So we look at the success of our European colleagues

754
00:38:55,070 --> 00:38:56,470
心中五味杂陈
with mixed feelings.

755
00:38:56,470 --> 00:38:59,170
就像是看着你的丈母娘
It's a little bit like watching your mother-in-law

756
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,840
开着你的"宝马"冲下悬崖
drive off a cliff in your BMW.

757
00:39:05,010 --> 00:39:07,010
(弗里曼)2008年9月
(Freeman) September 2008.

758
00:39:07,020 --> 00:39:10,120
物理学家们屏住呼吸
The physics world holds its collective breath

759
00:39:10,120 --> 00:39:14,990
LHC首次运转
as the LHC powers up for the first time.

760
00:39:14,990 --> 00:39:17,090
第一次低能量的粒子束
The first low-powered beams

761
00:39:17,090 --> 00:39:21,800
穿过17英里长的轨道 一切正常
shoot through the 17-mile ring,and all is well.

762
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:24,870
他们准备好揭开宇宙的面纱
They're ready to tear the veil off the Universe

763
00:39:24,870 --> 00:39:27,330
试图发现Higgs粒子
and try to catch sight of the Higgs.

764
00:39:27,340 --> 00:39:29,970
现在他们提高了能量—
Now they raise the power --

765
00:39:29,970 --> 00:39:34,740
达到7万亿电子伏特
one more notch on the way up to 7 trillion volts.

766
00:39:34,740 --> 00:39:36,380
然后...
And then...

767
00:39:38,350 --> 00:39:42,280
...LHC改变了
...The LHC explodes.

768
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:44,950
[ 爆炸]
[ Explosion ]

769
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:48,710
巨大的爆炸摧毁了
An enormous blast destroys

770
00:39:48,710 --> 00:39:51,710
几百个超导磁控管
hundreds of the superconducting magnets

771
00:39:51,710 --> 00:39:54,910
它们将质子束射过加速器
that shoot protons through the accelerator.

772
00:39:57,450 --> 00:39:59,750
-很戏剧性  -是的，必须的
It was pretty dramatic. Yeah,absolutely.

773
00:39:59,750 --> 00:40:01,180
花了一年的时间修复
It took a year to fix.

774
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:03,720
一道电弧
It must have been quite an electrical arc

775
00:40:03,720 --> 00:40:05,020
融化了—
to melt through the --

776
00:40:05,020 --> 00:40:06,190
想想那个打开门的
imagine the face of the guy

777
00:40:06,190 --> 00:40:07,560
哥们儿的表情吧
who opened the door to the tunnel.

778
00:40:07,560 --> 00:40:09,390
[ 笑 ]
[ Laughs ]

779
00:40:09,390 --> 00:40:12,130
吔，我能想象当时 等着进去的心情
Yeah,I can imagine waiting to get in there right then.

780
00:40:12,130 --> 00:40:14,260
他肯定非常非常紧张
He must have been really,really nervous

781
00:40:14,270 --> 00:40:15,370
想要看看发生什么事
to see what had happened.

782
00:40:15,370 --> 00:40:17,470
你知道，极其令人失望
You know,it was desperately disappointing

783
00:40:17,470 --> 00:40:19,340
每个参与的人都失望透了
for everyone involved.

784
00:40:19,340 --> 00:40:22,740
当CERN重建了坏掉的磁控管
As CERN rebuilds its broken magnets,

785
00:40:22,740 --> 00:40:26,310
费米实验室的加速器 已经追了上来
Fermilab's Tevatron steps up the pace.

786
00:40:26,310 --> 00:40:29,080
但他们没有发现Higgs粒子
But they don't see the Higgs.

787
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:32,680
这意味着Higgs粒子
This means that the Higgs particle,

788
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:36,020
携带着引力作用的粒子
the force carrier that allows matter to clump together,

789
00:40:36,020 --> 00:40:37,750
具有很高的质量
has a high mass,

790
00:40:37,760 --> 00:40:39,490
质量越大
and the higher the mass,

791
00:40:39,490 --> 00:40:43,030
意味着需要更大的能量来找到它
the more outside energy it takes to crack it open.

792
00:40:43,030 --> 00:40:48,100
费米实验室无法产生足够的能量
At this point,Fermilab just can't generate enough energy.

793
00:40:51,670 --> 00:40:57,210
2009年9月，CERN的LHC 重装上阵
December 2009. CERN's LHC restarts.

794
00:40:57,210 --> 00:41:02,550
几周内，它轻松超过 费米实验室的记录
Within weeks,it powers up well past Fermilab's capacity.

795
00:41:02,550 --> 00:41:07,280
甚至，它的威力有七倍之巨
Eventually,it will be 7 times more powerful.

796
00:41:08,650 --> 00:41:10,950
两台设备同时运转
With both machines running,

797
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:15,590
Higgs粒子也许会在 接下来几年内被发现
the Higgs particle could be found in the next few years,

798
00:41:15,590 --> 00:41:19,260
除非每个人的噩梦成真
unless everyone's secret fear comes true --

799
00:41:19,260 --> 00:41:22,330
如果没有Higgs粒子怎么办?
what if it's not there at all?

800
00:41:22,330 --> 00:41:25,170
如果标准模型是错的
What if the Standard Model is wrong

801
00:41:25,170 --> 00:41:29,040
Higgs粒子根本不存在怎么办？
and the Higgs doesn't exist?

802
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:34,010
如果实验证据足以证明
If it turns out that the experimental evidence

803
00:41:34,010 --> 00:41:36,350
没有这类东西
is strongly that there is no such thing,

804
00:41:36,350 --> 00:41:38,080
那我就太困惑了
then I'm simply baffled,

805
00:41:38,080 --> 00:41:41,420
因为那意味着许多物理学家
because it means that a great deal of physics,

806
00:41:41,420 --> 00:41:47,260
我认为我现在理解的东西 实际上我不再理解了
which I think I now understand,I would no longer understand.

807
00:41:47,260 --> 00:41:48,960
如果Higgs理论是错误的
If the Higgs theory is wrong,

808
00:41:48,960 --> 00:41:50,830
当然 很多理论物理学家
of course,many theoretical physicists

809
00:41:50,830 --> 00:41:52,830
会从二楼窗户跳下来的
will jump out of second-floor windows.

810
00:41:52,830 --> 00:41:55,530
那大概是他们去的最高的地方
That's about as high as they go.

811
00:41:55,530 --> 00:42:00,240
大自然知道它是如何运转
(Close) Nature knows how it works.

812
00:42:00,240 --> 00:42:03,310
很快，我们就会知道 它是如何运转的
Soon we will know how it works.

813
00:42:03,310 --> 00:42:05,780
我们有自己的理论解释它
We have our ideas on how it works,

814
00:42:05,780 --> 00:42:07,680
也许会被证明是正确的
which may be proved correct.

815
00:42:07,680 --> 00:42:10,610
也许会被证明是错误的
They may be proved wrong.

816
00:42:10,620 --> 00:42:13,250
无论如何，我们学到了东西
Whichever it is,we will learn.

817
00:42:13,250 --> 00:42:16,050
如果你问我押宝哪边
If you're asking me to place my bets,

818
00:42:16,050 --> 00:42:20,060
我认为类似Higgs玻色子的 某个东西是存在的
I think that something like the Higgs Boson is out there,

819
00:42:20,060 --> 00:42:21,890
等着我们发现它
waiting to be discovered.

820
00:42:21,890 --> 00:42:24,490
更激动人心的是，实际上
What would be more exciting is,in fact,

821
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:27,160
我们发现了自己不了解的东西
we find things that we don't understand.

822
00:42:27,170 --> 00:42:29,170
我们知道Higgs粒子会存在
So,we understand that the Higgs is gonna be there,

823
00:42:29,170 --> 00:42:30,700
所以我们发现它 加油，加油
and so we find it,so,hurray,hurray.

824
00:42:30,700 --> 00:42:31,900
现在我们做什么?
Now what do we do?

825
00:42:31,900 --> 00:42:33,340
但是如果你找到 你不了解的某物
But if you find something you don't understand,

826
00:42:33,340 --> 00:42:34,940
呃，现在人们有了个工作
well,now people have a job.

827
00:42:34,940 --> 00:42:36,940
我每天的工作就是
My job every day is to go to work

828
00:42:36,940 --> 00:42:39,610
上班去，去了解我不了解的东西
and understand things that I don' understand.

829
00:42:39,610 --> 00:42:42,250
如果我有更多的不了解的东西
If I have more stuff to no understand,

830
00:42:42,250 --> 00:42:43,610
那实际上是工作保险
that's job security.

831
00:42:49,420 --> 00:42:53,920
所以，我们由何组成？
So,what are we really made of?

832
00:42:53,930 --> 00:42:55,790
深入原子内部
Dig deep inside the atom,

833
00:42:55,790 --> 00:42:57,890
你会发现微小的粒子
and you will find tiny particles

834
00:42:57,900 --> 00:43:02,200
由浩瀚空间中的 不可见作用聚集起来
held together by invisible forces in a sea of empty space.

835
00:43:02,200 --> 00:43:03,700
更深入一步
Dig even further,

836
00:43:03,700 --> 00:43:08,310
我们发现万物都是由
and we discover that everything is made up of tiny packets

837
00:43:08,310 --> 00:43:11,270
从宇宙熔炉产生的 小团能量组成
of energy born in cosmic furnaces.

838
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:13,580
这些能量冷却下来
This energy that cools down

839
00:43:13,580 --> 00:43:18,150
被由Higgs粒子伴随的神秘作用
gets dragged through a mysterious force named the Higgs

840
00:43:18,150 --> 00:43:19,750
组合起来
and clumps together,

841
00:43:19,750 --> 00:43:23,250
组成我们称为物质的东西
forming all the things we call matter.

842
00:43:23,250 --> 00:43:26,820
它还有个邪恶的孪生兄弟 称为反物质
It has an evil twin called antimatter,

843
00:43:26,820 --> 00:43:30,830
但其中大部分早就消失了
but most of that has long since disappeared.

844
00:43:30,830 --> 00:43:35,400
当我们在加速器里
As we get closer to re-creating the heat of the big bang

845
00:43:35,400 --> 00:43:37,130
近乎重现大爆炸的核心
in our accelerators,

846
00:43:37,130 --> 00:43:38,640
我们也接近真相
we get closer to understanding

847
00:43:38,640 --> 00:43:41,910
明白这些是如何发生的
how and why all this happened.

848
00:43:41,910 --> 00:43:45,580
也许不久的将来
Perhaps some day not long from now,

849
00:43:45,580 --> 00:43:50,210
我们会最终解决物质之谜
we'll finally solve the last remaining riddles of matter

850
00:43:50,210 --> 00:43:56,120
完全理解创造的机制
and fully comprehend the inner workings of creation.

851
00:43:56,130 --> 00:44:01,030
-- 感谢观赏 --

